second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"24th Rifle Division was formed in which year?\", \"slot_hint\": \"year\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 21, \"text\": \"in Donbass from 2014.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00\", \"start\": 22, \"end\": 161, \"text\": \"Its Soviet honorifics were progressively removed and replaced with the King Danylo honorific following the beginning of the War in Donbass.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00\", \"start\": 162, \"end\": 323, \"text\": \"The division was formed on the order of the Revolutionary Military Council on July 26, 1918, from voluntary groups under the name 1st Simbirsk Infantry Division.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00\", \"start\": 324, \"end\": 392, \"text\": \"In November 1918 it was renamed as the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00\", \"start\": 393, \"end\": 526, \"text\": \"It actively participated in the Russian Civil War in the Volga region, in the Southern Urals Mountains, and in Polissya and Volhynia.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00\", \"start\": 527, \"end\": 615, \"text\": \"At this time one of its regimental commanders was a future Army General Maksim Purkayev.\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 21, \"text\": \"in Donbass from 2014.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01\", \"start\": 22, \"end\": 161, \"text\": \"Its Soviet honorifics were progressively removed and replaced with the King Danylo honorific following the beginning of the War in Donbass.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01\", \"start\": 162, \"end\": 325, \"text\": \"The division was formed on the order of the Revolutionary Military Council on January 1, 1920, from voluntary groups under the name 1st Simbirsk Infantry Division.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01\", \"start\": 326, \"end\": 394, \"text\": \"In November 1920 it was renamed as the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01\", \"start\": 395, \"end\": 528, \"text\": \"It actively participated in the Russian Civil War in the Volga region, in the Southern Urals Mountains, and in Polissya and Volhynia.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01\", \"start\": 529, \"end\": 617, \"text\": \"At this time one of its regimental commanders was a future Army General Maksim Purkayev.\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 78, \"text\": \"regiment, one Guards training artillery regiment and one air defence regiment.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d02\", \"start\": 79, \"end\": 258, \"text\": \"These units were the 70th, 71st and 72nd Motor Rifle Regiments; the 392nd Tank Regiment; the 50th Guards Training Artillery Regiment and the 1203rd Anti-aircraft Missile Regiment.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d02\", \"start\": 259, \"end\": 321, \"text\": \"In November 1990 it had a total of 219 tanks, 187 being T-55s.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d02\", \"start\": 322, \"end\": 364, \"text\": \"It was disbanded on 4 January 1992 (Holm).\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d02\", \"start\": 365, \"end\": 480, \"text\": \"Later it may have had to hand over half its weapons to the Chechens in order to evacuate the other half unhindered.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d02\", \"start\": 481, \"end\": 530, \"text\": \"The Division did not reform until the late 1990s.\"}, \"D3S7\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d02\", \"start\": 531, \"end\": 587, \"text\": \"Following the beginning of the Second Chechen War it was\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 92, \"text\": \"following World War II , it seems to have become 42nd Guards MRD in 1957 , while at Grozny .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d03\", \"start\": 93, \"end\": 286, \"text\": \"In 1987 it became 173 Guards District Training Centre , and it comprised in 1991 of three Motor Rifle Regiments , one Tank rgt , one Guards Training Artillery rgt and one Air-Defense regiment .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d03\", \"start\": 287, \"end\": 351, \"text\": \"In November 1990 it had a total of 219 tanks , 187 being T-55s .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d03\", \"start\": 352, \"end\": 512, \"text\": \"By June 1993 173 Guards Training Centre had been disbanded and had handed over half its weapons to the Chechens in order to evacuate the other half unhindered .\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d03\", \"start\": 513, \"end\": 516, \"text\": \"The\"}, \"D5S1\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d04\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 45, \"text\": \"of the 12th Army Corps , on 18 October 1960 .\"}, \"D5S2\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d04\", \"start\": 46, \"end\": 218, \"text\": \"Training centre 1987–1992 Summarize Perspective 1986 Structure of the 42nd Motor Rifle Division On 14 September 1987 , it became the 173rd Guards District Training Centre .\"}, \"D5S3\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d04\", \"start\": 219, \"end\": 426, \"text\": \"[ 2 ] In 1991 , it comprised the 70th , 71st , and 72nd Motor Rifle Regiments ; the 392nd Tank Regiment at Shali ; the 50th Guards Training Artillery Regiment ; and the 1203rd Anti-aircraft Rocket Regiment .\"}, \"D5S4\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d04\", \"start\": 427, \"end\": 482, \"text\": \"In November 1990 , it had 219 tanks , 187 being T-55s .\"}, \"D5S5\": {\"document_number\": 5, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d04\", \"start\": 483, \"end\": 528, \"text\": \"From September to December 1991 , part of the\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"24th Rifle Division\", \"scope\": \"formation year\", \"claim\": \"The 24th Rifle Division was formed in 1918.\", \"answer\": \"1918\", \"quote\": \"The division was formed on the order of the Revolutionary Military Council on July 26, 1918, from voluntary groups under the name 1st Simbirsk Infantry Division. In November 1918 it was renamed as the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0190-dd2bafd181cc:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"24th Rifle Division\", \"scope\": \"formation year\", \"claim\": \"The 24th Rifle Division was formed in 1920.\", \"answer\": \"1920\", \"quote\": \"The division was formed on the order of the Revolutionary Military Council on January 1, 1920, from voluntary groups under the name 1st Simbirsk Infantry Division. In November 1920 it was renamed as the 24th Simbirsk Rifle Division.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"1918\", \"1920\"],